</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Phelan</surname><given-names>PE</given-names><suffix>3rd</suffix></name><name><surname>Witten</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name><name><surname>Mellon</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Pathogenesis and inflammatory response to Edwardsiella tarda infection in the zebrafish.</article-title><source>Dev Comp Immunol</source><volume>29</volume><fpage>501</fpage><lpage>513</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15752547</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000463-Lesley1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lesley</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ramakrishnan</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Insights into early mycobacterial pathogenesis from the zebrafish.</article-title><source>Curr Opin Microbiol</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>283</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18571973</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000463-vanderSar1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>van der Sar</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Appelmelk</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Vandenbroucke-Grauls</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bitter</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>A star with stripes: zebrafish as an infection model.</article-title><source>Trends Microbiol</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>451</fpage><lpage>457</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15381194</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000463-Clay1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clay</surna